  body: "# Bereavement Support Payment regime and source qualifications\n\n## Authored interpretation\n\nThe BSP
    chapter identifies 6 April 2017 as its introductory death-date boundary and contrasts it with the earlier Bereavement
    Benefit and Widow’s Benefits regimes.\n\n## Scope and exceptions\n\nDMG 59001 and 59011 refer to Memo 02/23.
    Their spouse/civil-partner wording must be read with chapter 63 Appendix 1 on the 2023 remedial order and higher-rate
    BSP for specified surviving cohabiting partners with dependent children. The project does not infer present
    eligibility from the introduction alone.\n\n## Inspected passages\n\n- [DMG 59001, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 59002, PDF page 2](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=2).\n\
    - [DMG 59011, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=5).\n\
    \n## Additional context\n\n- [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 32](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=32).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 33](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=33).\n\
    - [Context: chapter 63, PDF page 40](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68efa22be7b6794c076bbec0/dmg-v-10-ch-63.pdf#page=40).\n\
    \n## Evidence and review status\n\nIndependent experimental interpretation of captured DWP guidance, not an
    official DWP document. Definitions and semantic associations are model-assisted proposals awaiting specialist
    review. No individual entitlement decision, medical conclusion, award calculation or executable rule is provided.\n\
    \nSource observation, listing-page update, printed revision, legal event and claimant-event dates are separate.
    Current legal applicability is unresolved. Page numbers are one-based PDF positions; machine extraction may
    damage reading order, characters and footnotes. No visual PDF or specialist acceptance is claimed.\n\n- `dmg-vol10-ch59`:
    PDF `71e82cafa85c42d01158e79ffef2753cee93cbf6f70ca25e1f51a3e5e13e5192`; extracted pages `495f463962f1954952a4c175629d05ea9edda5403a3e95cb44d4ce64414beb61`;
    acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.706049Z`.\n- `dmg-vol10-ch63`: PDF `7f894b8bac8a4056f9b89fff0df4cdb4231c1c2b187de78b5c64b6cc33636d88`;
    extracted pages `ed410bfb75f7f3ac15120a0dd10024bfb246faea02695229229deaed09d9033e`; acquired `2026-09-15T19:45:32.914779Z`.\n"
  resource: https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/63e64acce90e0706cd61fb95/dmgch59.pdf#page=2
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/bereavement-benefit-regime
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source distinguishes pre-6 April 2017 bereavement rules and continuing awards from the BSP
      regime.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch59/0002
      quote: "59002 A person whose\n\n\n1. spouse dies on or after 9.4.01 or\n\n\n2. civil partner dies on or after
        5.12.05\n\n\nbut before 6.4.17 can claim BB (see DMG Chapter 63). Also, people already receiving BB on 5.4.17
        can\ncontinue to receive it for as long as the qualifying conditions apply. A person who continues to receive\n\
        BB after 5.4.17 can also get BSP if their second spouse/civil partner dies on or after 6.4.17.\n\n\nNote:
        See DMG Chapter 58 for guidance where the death was before 9.4.01."
      locator: DMG 59002
  - target: term/bsp-remarriage-treatment
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The source expressly contrasts BSP treatment of remarriage/new partnerships with WB and BB.
    evidence:
    - page: page/dmg-vol10-ch59/0004
      quote: "59007 Unlike WB and BB, a person will continue to receive BSP if they\n\n\n1. remarry or\n\n\n2. form
        a civil partnership or\n\n\n3. start LTAMC."
      locator: DMG 59007
